From b6eecbad057030c47b18417b5aa81ca005000b33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:03:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(worker-boards): only ENOENT is missing in every
 inventory existence check

Path.exists() is version-dependent: Python 3.14+ returns False on any
OSError, while 3.11-3.13 (still allowed by requires-python) raise e.g.
PermissionError. On 3.14 an unsearchable worker-resources/ made paths()
silently drop every registered board from the capacity census.

- worker_board_retirement.missing(): stat + except FileNotFoundError, the
  single shared helper (worker_account_boards._missing now aliases it), with
  a docstring stating the version-specific behaviour.
- paths(): default/boards/worker-resources checks and the named-board file
  check use it; an unreadable location raises instead of returning a census
  without its boards.
- register() destination, removing() record/path checks, retirement
  pending()/recover() use it. removing()'s finally treats an unreadable path
  as not removed (keeps the record) instead of masking the original error.
- discard(): unlink + except FileNotFoundError (no check/unlink race).
- Tests: os.stat EACCES on each inventory location -> paths() raises;
  unreadable record -> register() raises; missing()/discard() ENOENT-only.
  The vanished-record test uses record_paths() instead of hard-coding the
  sha256 naming; function-local imports moved to module level.

Follow-up to PR #1877 review nits 1-3.
